              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "tnkPo",
              "name": "Rules",
              "width": "fill_container",
              "fill": "$bg",
              "cornerRadius": 10,
              "stroke": "$border",
              "strokeWidth": 1,
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": 8,
              "padding": 24,
              "children": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "szlWe",
                  "name": "Title",
                  "fill": "$fg",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "Worst-case rules",
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 15,
                  "fontWeight": "600"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Q5pc4",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Model names wrap to two lines in the menu, and end-truncate in the chip at 240px. The full name is in the chip's tooltip.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "Ef7os",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Chips never wrap. At narrow widths the key hint goes first, then the Where chip shrinks to its icon.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "jAUig",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• The menu caps at the space above the composer and scrolls, with Refresh pinned at the bottom.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "CmTlW",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• A missing plan reads “ChatGPT account” or “Claude subscription”, never blank. Versions end-truncate after 16 characters.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "EJFbQ",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• An effort Newjen doesn't know is shown as the CLI names it, capitalised (“Minimal”).",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "id": "QUv2o",
                  "name": "Rule",
                  "fill": "$fg-muted",
                  "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "content": "• Reset times: “2:20am” today, “tomorrow 2:20am”, then “Thu 9:14am”. Never a countdown that ticks.",
                  "lineHeight": 1.55,
                  "fontFamily": "$font",
                  "fontSize": 13,
                  "fontWeight": "normal"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "frame",
      "id": "sGbDk",
      "x": 1400,
      "y": 8339,
      "name": "Decisions · agent and model picker",
      "theme": {
        "mode": "dark"
      },
      "width": 560,
      "fill": "$bg",
      "cornerRadius": 10,
      "stroke": "$border",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "layout": "vertical",
      "gap": 10,
      "padding": 28,
      "children": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "jmG0t",
          "name": "Title",
          "fill": "$fg",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "Agent and model picker — decisions",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 16,
          "fontWeight": "600"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Ppz2v",
          "name": "Item 1",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Where: the composer footer, next to Rift's Where chip: [Where] [Agent · Model] [Effort]. Same place as T3 Code, the Codex app and Cursor: you pick the model where you type.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "auMfP",
          "name": "Item 2",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Agent menu: Claude | Codex tabs, then that agent's models. One agent per thread, so the tabs make the choice explicit and keep each list short. A tab's dot shows ready, needs attention or unavailable.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CB993",
          "name": "Item 3",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Before you send, each tab shows the plan and who pays. Warnings sit at the top of the tab: API key billing, plan used up so credits pay, a CLI older than tested.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "tkBzA",
          "name": "Item 4",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• After the first message the choice is frozen, and the chips become a plain label (“Codex · GPT-6.1-Sol · XHigh”). No switching mid-thread for now.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "yMPWQ",
          "name": "Item 5",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Effort lists only the efforts that model offers. Default leaves effort to the CLI. Fast is a switch using the provider's own words; Claude's warns that it may bill extra usage. A model left on Default keeps effort on Default and speed on normal.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "lFO0J",
          "name": "Item 6",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• New threads start with the last choice you sent in this project. The very first one uses the first ready agent with its CLI defaults.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "sa46c",
          "name": "Item 7",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Detection runs at launch, on Refresh, and when the menu opens if the last check is over 5 minutes old. It never polls in the background and never spends usage.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "CTgJa",
          "name": "Item 8",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Limits: credits paying shows a warning and the turn goes ahead. A refused limit stops the thread, shows the reset time and pauses sending until then. Newjen never retries or resumes on its own.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "DEGvM",
          "name": "Item 9",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Email and organisation stay hidden. Clicking the plan line shows them.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "RQKo4",
          "name": "Item 10",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Motion: opened by keyboard, menus appear with no animation. Opened by click, a 120ms fade plus scale from 0.98, starting from the chip. Switching tabs and changing labels don't animate.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "Le3lv",
          "name": "Item 11",
          "fill": "$fg-muted",
          "textGrowth": "fixed-width",
          "width": "fill_container",
          "content": "• Keys: ↑↓ move, ←→ switch tabs, ↵ choose, esc close. Tab moves between the chips.",
          "lineHeight": 1.55,
          "fontFamily": "$font",
          "fontSize": 13,
          "fontWeight": "normal"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
